Subject: [PATCH] inetcomm: address tables, schema, security, message tree,
 offset tables, range lists, IMAP, SMTP/POP3 additions

Closes the 104 gap-A items of inetcomm.

mimeaddr.c: IMimeAddressTable over the address headers of a body (all methods, header
write-back, header changes seen), IMimeEnumAddressTypes (filled in mimeole.idl), registered
address types, MimeGetAddressFormatW, the address calls of IMimeMessage.
mimeole.c: read-only sub_stream (Clone, Stat, locks), IMimeBody options and cert bags,
IsType/GetTransmitInfo/BindToObject, global IMimePropertySchema used by new properties,
IMimeSecurity certificate and message-type calls, ToMultipart, MoveBody, ResolveURL,
Set/GetCharset, SetTextBody (alternatives), AttachFile/URL/Object, Commit, HandsOffStorage,
Load/SaveOffsetTable, aggregation refused.
rangelist.c: IRangeList and CreateRangeList.
imaptransport.c: IIMAPTransport commands and the responses of RFC 3501, run from the
transport window; sequence-number table; LOGIN through OnLogonPrompt.
smtptransport.c, pop3transport.c, internettransport.c, protocol.c: CommandDOT, dot-stuffed
SendDataStream, SetWindow/ResetWindow, SendMessage2, CommandRCPT2 NOTIFY, MarkItem,
CommandAUTH, IsState; mhtml Seek/Abort/LockRequest.

Not done (ESCALATE.md): S/MIME crypto, CreateWebPage/GetRootMoniker/SplitMessage,
InetServerFromAccount. Guessed values are listed in patches/notes/3200.txt.

